  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Unseasonably mild through Friday with 2.5 weeks-\nlong dry spell now over.\n\nAnomalous upper level ridging and south-southwest flow aloft\nwill maintain unseasonably warm temperatures through late week.\nHigh temps this afternoon will make it into the mid 70s across \nmuch of central PA, still 15 to 20 degrees above average. Highs\nwill be about 5 to 10 degrees cooler on Friday.\n\nThe cold front responsible for the rain this morning will slow\ndown or stall near the I95 corridor tonight. A dry slot will \nkeep most locations dry this afternoon into Friday, but a weak\nwave along the front may trigger another round of showers this\nevening in the Lower Susq Valley later this afternoon into the\nevening.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Trending cooler this weekend with lake enhanced \nrain showers beneath upper level low\n\nSeasonably cooler/breezy pattern to start the first full \nweekend of November. The passage of closed H5 low followed by \nmean cyclonic flow favors persistent clouds and periods of lake\nenhanced rain over the western and central Alleghenies on \nSaturday. We were keen to manually adjust max temps a few\ndegrees lower on 11/7 to account for the cooler pattern shift\nwhich looks to continue into early next week. If the current\nforecast holds, it will be the first below average daytime high\nin three weeks!",
